        <body>
            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TRO01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>John Bernard</forename>
                        <surname>Trotter</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1775-12-26">
                        <placeName>Northern Ireland</placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1818-09-29"/>
                    <occupation>author</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The 1800 entries are during Godwin’s trip to Ireland and therefore the
    attribution seems probable. There is also some correspondence in 1803. Equally the  1806 entries imply that Trotter is in London and indeed it was during this year that he served as 
    private secretary to <persName key="FOX01">Charles James Fox</persName>. In 1818, he is calling on Longman for Trotter and writing to Trotter. It is possible
    he was negotiating on his behalf for a new edition of <title>Walks through Ireland</title>, published in 1819 by Sir R Phillips.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS. Abinger c. 15, fols. 82-3: 4 Dec.; MS. Abinger c. 8, fol. 27-8: 9 July 1803</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
